(version 1)

# Transformer-secondary isolation barrier.
#
# /BLACK and /RED are the 120 V transformer secondary, brought out on J1.
# IPC-2221B table 6-1 column B2 (external conductors, uncoated, sea level to
# 3050 m) asks for 1.25 mm at 151-300 V working; 1.5 mm covers that and is the
# usual target for a 120 V mains-referenced circuit. The 11-14 V input, the
# 21.75 V bus and the 3v3/1V1 logic rails are all far below 151 V, so the
# 0.18 mm default netclass clearance is correct everywhere else.
# /PE (J5 pins 3/4, outlet earth) has no routed copper on this board; if a
# later revision routes it, give it its own isolation rule -- the 0.18 mm
# default is not enough for an earth fault-current path near /BLACK//RED.
#
# This rule is what pulls the GND pour back from the secondary. Refill the
# zones after editing copper, or the plotted pour will not obey it.
(rule "secondary isolation 1.5mm"
  (constraint clearance (min 1.5mm))
  (condition "A.NetName == '/BLACK' || A.NetName == '/RED' || B.NetName == '/BLACK' || B.NetName == '/RED'"))

# Mouse-bite panel tabs MTB1-3: NPTH breakaway holes sit on the board edge
# and intentionally violate the board-wide 0.2mm hole-to-copper rule.
# Copper pullback around bites is ~0.125mm, fine for tab-route breakout.
# No MTB footprints are placed on the board as submitted; the rule is kept
# for panelisation.
(rule "mousebite hole clearance"
  (condition "A.Reference == 'MTB*' || B.Reference == 'MTB*'")
  (constraint hole_clearance (min 0.1mm)))
